  "name": "Corrupting touch",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/magic/unholy/strike-hand-glow-pink.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>Grapples one humanoid, animal or nature creature and transfers 50% of the caster's current Corruption to it.</p><p>The caster tests Strength + 10 against the target's Strength.</p><p><strong>On success:</strong> the target is grappled. While the caster holds it, the caster generates 3d10 Corruption per round and transfers it directly.</p><p>The target may spend an Action to attempt to escape, which triggers a Strength versus test. Casting this spell provokes an Opportunity Attack, and the grapple only begins if the target fails to defend against it.</p>",
